---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import SidebarDemo from '../../components/SidebarDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs title="Sidebar">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Sidebar</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A home for your navigation. Collapsible groups, an icon rail, and a mobile drawer, built with Base UI.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <SidebarDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Sidebar usage"
      code={`import {
  Sidebar, SidebarProvider, SidebarContent,
  SidebarGroup, SidebarMenu, SidebarMenuItem,
  SidebarMenuButton, SidebarTrigger,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/sidebar";

<SidebarProvider className="min-h-dvh">
  <Sidebar label="Main navigation">
    <SidebarContent>
      <SidebarGroup>
        <SidebarMenu>
          <SidebarMenuItem>
            <SidebarMenuButton
              icon={<HomeIcon />}
              nativeButton={false}
              render={<a href="/overview" />}
              isActive
            >
              Overview
            </SidebarMenuButton>
          </SidebarMenuItem>
        </SidebarMenu>
      </SidebarGroup>
    </SidebarContent>
  </Sidebar>
  <main className="min-w-0 flex-1">
    <SidebarTrigger />
    {children}
  </main>
</SidebarProvider>`}
    />
    <p>
      Supply icons from your own icon library. Use the <code>render</code> prop with your router's link and{' '}
      <code>nativeButton={false}</code> for navigation. Use a normal button for actions.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Parts</h2>
    <p>
      <code>SidebarProvider</code> owns open state. <code>Sidebar</code> handles the panel and mobile drawer.{' '}
      <code>SidebarHeader</code> and <code>SidebarFooter</code> stay visible while <code>SidebarContent</code> scrolls.
      Put a<code>SidebarInput</code> in the header to search or filter the menu; it is an{' '}
      <a href="/components/input/">Input</a> on the canvas color.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>SidebarGroup</code> and <code>SidebarGroupLabel</code> organize a <code>SidebarMenu</code>. Each{' '}
      <code>SidebarMenuItem</code> contains a <code>SidebarMenuButton</code>, with optional <code>icon</code>,{' '}
      <code>badge</code>, <code>isActive</code>, and <code>tooltip</code> props. Give complex labels an explicit{' '}
      <code>aria-label</code> or <code>tooltip</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>SidebarMenuAction</code> adds a separate action. <code>SidebarSection</code> combines a navigation link with
      an independent disclosure button. Put <code>SidebarMenuSubItem</code> and <code>SidebarMenuSubButton</code> inside
      it. For a custom composition, use <code>SidebarMenuSub</code> directly.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Nested navigation</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Nested navigation"
      code={`<SidebarSection
  label="Projects"
  icon={<FolderIcon />}
  nativeButton={false}
  render={<a href="/projects" />}
  defaultOpen
>
  <SidebarMenuSubItem>
    <SidebarMenuSubButton
      nativeButton={false}
      render={<a href="/projects/website" />}
    >
      Website refresh
    </SidebarMenuSubButton>
  </SidebarMenuSubItem>
</SidebarSection>`}
    />
    <p>
      The label navigates; the arrow expands. Collapsing the whole sidebar hides nested links without forgetting which
      sections were open. Sections also accept <code>open</code> and <code>onOpenChange</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">State and layout</h2>
    <p>
      <code>Sidebar</code> supports <code>side="left"</code> or <code>"right"</code>, and{' '}
      <code>collapsible="icon"</code>, <code>"offcanvas"</code>, or <code>"none"</code>. Put a right sidebar after your
      content in the DOM. The provider follows its container's height; give it a viewport height or a bounded preview
      height.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>SidebarProvider</code> accepts <code>defaultOpen</code>, or controlled <code>open</code> /{' '}
      <code>onOpenChange</code>. Mobile state is separate through <code>openMobile</code> /{' '}
      <code>onOpenMobileChange</code>. <code>useSidebar()</code> exposes these states, their setters,{' '}
      <code>isMobile</code>, <code>state</code>, and <code>toggleSidebar()</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Saving preferences belongs to the application. This preview stores its open state in local storage; the package
      never writes cookies or storage. For server rendering, pass your saved preference as <code>defaultOpen</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Behavior and accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Below 768px, collapsible sidebars become modal drawers. Base UI handles focus trapping, Escape dismissal, and
      scroll locking. Links close the drawer; custom navigation handlers can call <code>setOpenMobile(false)</code>. A
      visible Close action is always provided.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tab follows normal link order. Enter activates links; Enter or Space toggles disclosures. Icon-only items keep
      accessible names and show tooltips on hover or focus. Set <code>keyboardShortcut={false}</code> on the provider to
      disable Cmd/Ctrl+B. The shortcut does not run inside editable fields.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>SidebarMenuSkeleton</code> provides a static loading row. <code>SidebarSeparator</code> draws an inset line
      between groups. Your application supplies loading announcements, empty messages, error messages, and retry
      actions. Routes, permissions, workspace switchers, account menus, and data fetching are not part of the package.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
